# The learning store is append-mostly JSONL: two branches that each record a
# lesson append at EOF and would always conflict. A union merge keeps both
# sides of every conflicting hunk instead. Costs of that choice:
# - Only readers that go through learn.ScanStore (pkg/learn and
#   pkg/memindex) merge the copies: a line kept twice, or two versions of a
#   rewritten lesson (same id and timestamp), read as one, the version with
#   the higher reuse_count. Anything that reads the file raw, such as a
#   prompt context profile, sees the duplicated lines.
# - Prune resurrection: a lesson one branch pruned comes back when the other
#   branch rewrote the same line (MarkReused).
# - Reuse undercount: when both branches incremented the same lesson, the
#   higher count wins rather than the sum.
# - Two lessons with the same old-form id (L-NNN from an `auto` older than
#   the id suffix) and different timestamps are both kept; `auto checklist
#   status` warns about them.
.autopus/learnings/pipeline.jsonl merge=union
